Rāma notes agitation among Citrakūṭa ascetics --- Rāma asks Kulapati if fault lies in him --- Rāma asks if Lakṣmaṇa or Sītā offended seers --- Kulapati clears Sītā and blames Rāvaṇa kin Khara --- Kulapati says Janasthāna scourge shows dreadful forms since Rāma came --- Fiends befoul ladles douse fires and crush jars --- Seers urge leaving for nearby fruitful old āśrama --- Kulapati warns Khara threatens Rāma household too --- Rāma cannot detain eager Kulapati with replies --- Kulapati departs with hosts as Rāma settles home
